'' TKO0617, fbc's 119 (T18): assigning to a 'byref ... as const' parameter by name --
'' long, a UDT, string and ustring, '=' and '&=' -- is refused, as fbc refuses it. Only a
'' field write ('p.x = 1') was caught; the rest wrote through the reference into the
'' caller's variable. A byval const parameter, 'mid( s, ... ) =' and 'swap' were caught
'' already; a non-const byref parameter and a method's own field stay writable. Lines
'' identical to fbc-modern's errors. See CheckAssignTarget_ in symbols/assigntarget.bas.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/byref-const-param-write.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: byref-const-param-write.bas(5,5): error TKO0617
'' EXPECT-OUT: byref-const-param-write.bas(8,6): error TKO0617
'' EXPECT-OUT: byref-const-param-write.bas(11,5): error TKO0617
'' EXPECT-OUT: byref-const-param-write.bas(14,5): error TKO0617
'' EXPECT-OUT: byref-const-param-write.bas(17,5): error TKO0617
